icated obese women: comparison of indices from fasting and oral glucose load with euglycemic hyperinsulinemic clamp</article-title><source>Nutr Metab Cardiovasc Dis</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>366</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15853121</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0939-4753(04)80027-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pasimeni</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ribaudo</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Capoccia</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertone</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Leonetti</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Santiemma</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Non-invasive evaluation of endothelial dysfunction in uncomplicated obesity: Relationship with insulin resistance</article-title><source>Microvasc Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16434062</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.mvr.2005.12.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karelis</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Brochu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabasa-Lhoret</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Can we identify metabolically healthy but obese individuals (MHO)?</article-title><source>Diabetes Metab</source><year>2004</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>569</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671927</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1262-3636(07)70156-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person